{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["You shall celebrate it — a ḥataf qamatz is found in scrolls of other lands and it is the superior reading, for from the root חגג one says תְּחָגֻּהוּ — like from סבב, יְסָבֻּהוּ עֲרָבִי נָחַל. But תְּחַגֻּהוּ with a pataḥ is from the conjugation of the hollow letters, for from כלה one says תְּכַלּוּהוּ; from צוה, תְּצַוּוּהוּ."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The distinction Rashbam draws is between a qamatz qatan form (תְּחָגֻּהוּ, from geminate חגג) and a pataḥ form (תְּחַגֻּהוּ, from hollow חוג/חיג); 'ה\"י' refers to hollow verbs (נפ\"י / ע\"י), here rendered 'the hollow letters.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:13.297947587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}